    "shift": "unknown_shift"
  },
  "question": {
    "text": "If&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math>&nbsp;is the magnetic field at the centre of a circular loop of area&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;its magnetic dipole moment is&nbsp;found to be <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi><mfrac><mrow><mi>B</mi><msup><mi>A</mi><mi>m</mi></msup></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><msqrt><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">π</mi></msqrt></mrow></mfrac></math>, then what is the value of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>m</mi></math>?"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "3.5",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Let r be the radius of the circular loop.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo><mo>&#160;&#160;</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>&#960;</mi><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mi>&#960;</mi></mfrac></msqrt></math></p><p>Magnetic field at the centre of the loop is</p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>&#956;</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mi>I</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>r</mi></mrow></mfrac></math><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></math></p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>&#956;</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><msqrt><mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mi>&#960;</mi></mfrac></msqrt></mrow></mfrac><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></mrow><msub><mi>&#956;</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mfrac><msqrt><mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mi>&#960;</mi></mfrac></msqrt></math><p>Now, magnetic moment of the loop is</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>IA</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></mrow><msub><mi>&#956;</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mfrac><msqrt><mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mi>&#960;</mi></mfrac></msqrt><mo>&#183;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math></p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></mrow><msub><mi>&#956;</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mfrac><mfrac><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></msup><msqrt><mi>&#960;</mi></msqrt></mfrac></math><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math> and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn></math></p>"
  }
}